```javascript
function mapDistinct(items, keyOf, transform) {
  const negativeZero = Symbol("negativeZero");
  const cache = new Map();
  const results = [];
  const length = items.length;

  for (let index = 0; index < length; index++) {
    const item = items[index];
    const key = keyOf(item, index);
    const cacheKey = Object.is(key, -0) ? negativeZero : key;

    if (!cache.has(cacheKey)) {
      cache.set(cacheKey, transform(item, index));
    }

    results.push(cache.get(cacheKey));
  }

  return results;
}
```

Processes the input array in order, transforming only the first item for each distinct key. A private symbol distinguishes `-0` from `+0`; `Map` otherwise provides the required equality.

All results—including `undefined`, objects, and promises—are cached unchanged, preserving identity. Exceptions propagate immediately without alteration. The function itself never modifies the input array or its objects.
